jobs.description:
Are you strong in planning, organizing, and maintaining oversight in a dynamic logistics environment? Do you enjoy improving processes while supporting a fast-growing operation? Then the role of Operations Planner in Moerdijk could be your next career move. Working in one of the largest and most modern warehouses in the Benelux, you will play a crucial role in ensuring the smooth flow of daily order operations. You will make sure everything behind the scenes is perfectly coordinated, allowing the operation to perform at its best.

As an Operations Planner, you will be responsible for the warehouse's outbound planning activities. You will ensure that customer orders are properly prepared, scheduled, and processed within the operation. Working closely with the operational teams, you will act as a key link between systems, planning, and execution.

Your responsibilities include:

- Processing daily customer requests and forecasts;
- Planning and prioritizing outbound orders within the system;
- Aligning capacity and operational activities with the warehouse floor;
- Coordinating pick-and-pack processes to ensure orders are processed efficiently;
- Acting as the first point of contact for operational planning-related questions;
- Monitoring the progress, timing, and accuracy of order flows;
- Ensuring that all process steps are followed strictly from start to finish;
- Supporting the optimization of planning and logistics processes.

For this position, we are looking for someone who excels at planning and can maintain a clear overview in a complex logistics environment.

- Relevant experience within logistics (planning and/or warehouse operations);
- Strong organizational and administrative skills;
- Ability to work under pressure and effectively prioritize tasks;
- Good command of the English language (required);
- Comfortable working with computers and digital systems;
- Available to work full-time in a two-shift schedule.

As a Forklift and/or Reach Truck Operator, you are responsible for keeping the warehouse and shipping process running efficiently. Your daily tasks include collecting and moving goods, scanning shipments, checking orders for accuracy, loading and unloading trucks, and maintaining a clean and safe working environment. You are also happy to support other departments whenever needed, because teamwork is at the heart of DSV.

You will work full-time (40 hours per week) in a fixed team at the Moerdijk warehouse and are willing to work in a two-shift schedule.

- Valid Forklift and/or Reach Truck certificate;
- At least 1 year of experience operating a forklift or reach truck;
- Full-time availability (40 hours per week) willing to work a fixed two-shift schedule (06:00 - 15:00, 07:00 - 16:00, 08:00 - 17:00, or 15:00 - 00:00);
- Own transportation and willingness to work in Moerdijk;
- You are at least 18 years old and a VMBO or MBO working thinking level (or equivalent);
- You have a good command of the English language;
- Accurate, safety-conscious, and a team player;

Are you looking for an active job with variety in your tasks? FedEx in Duiven is looking for logistic employees. Your job is to make sure that all packages will reach their destination in time.

Your hourly salary can be €19,51 including shift allowance.

What are you going to do?
In this dynamic role, you'll ensure the smooth running of the sorting process. Your duties include:

• Sorting and processing incoming packages;

• Efficiently loading packages onto trucks;

• Collaborating with colleagues to meet deadlines.

You'll work the following shifts:

2:30 PM – 11:00 PM

5:30 PM – 1:00 AM

11:00 PM – 7:00 AM

What do we offer?
• Gross hourly wage of €15.01, with allowances up to €19.51 per hour;

• Prospects of permanent employment with FedEx;

• 8% holiday allowance and 25 vacation days;

• Travel allowance of €0.23 per kilometer;

• Pension accrual through Adecco from age 18;

• Access to the Adecco Academy for training and courses;

• A pleasant, safe work environment with dedicated colleagues.

Where will you work?
FedEx is one of the world's largest logistics service providers, shipping millions of packages daily from Duiven to over 200 countries. Working safely, collaborating, and continuously growing are our top priorities. Your efforts are recognized and appreciated.

What do we ask?
• You speak Dutch or English fluently;

• You can apply for a Certificate of Conduct (costs will be reimbursed);

• You have your own transportation;

• You can be deployed flexible.

Are you interested?
Ready to get started? Click the application button and take the next step in your career!

Questions? Send a message or call Sanne at 06 42506892. You can apply for this position until September 27th, 2026.

Are you experienced in a warehouse and ready to take the next step into a leadership role? Or do you already have some experience in supervising colleagues and want to further develop yourself as a team leader? Then this is your opportunity! Within a fast-growing and international logistics environment, you will have the opportunity to further develop your leadership skills and  take on more responsibility step by step.

As a (junior) Warehouse Team Leader, you will work alongside an experienced team and supervise a group of 10 to 12 employees. You will be visibly present on the work floor, supporting the daily coordination of operations. You work closely with the Supervisor and be given the space to grow in your role.

Your responsibilities include:

- Supporting the supervision and guidance of warehouse employees;
- Working on the floor to ensure smooth daily operations;
- Identifying operational bottlenecks and discussing them with your manager;
- Contributing to the improvement of work processes;
- Monitoring basic safety and quality regulations ;
- Working with simple reports and developing basic Excel skills.

We are primarily looking for someone with the right motivation and ambition to grow into a leadership role within logistics. In addition, you have:

- Experience in a warehouse or logistics environment;
- Interest in supervising or guiding colleagues;
- Good command of the English language (required);
- Basic knowledge of Excel or willingness to learn;
- A proactive and eager-to-learn attitude;
- Availability to work full-time in a two-shift system.

Have you not yet held a full team leader position, but do you have ambition and some initial experience in leading others? We strongly encourage you to apply.

Are you passionate about quality, compliance and continuous improvement?Do you enjoy optimizing processes and ensuring that quality standards are maintained throughout an organization? Then this position as Quality Specialist could be the perfect next step in your career.

What will you do?

As a Quality Specialist, you will be responsible for managing, maintaining and continuously improving the Quality Management System (QMS). You will support site management, ensure compliance with customer and regulatory requirements, and help create a strong quality culture across the organization.

Your responsibilities include:

- Planning, implementing and maintaining the Quality Management System (QMS);
- Ensuring quality governance and compliance across logistics operations;
- Promoting a strong culture of quality and continuous improvement;
- Coordinating internal and external audits and following up on improvement actions;
- Monitoring customer, legal and third-party quality requirements;
- Identifying improvement opportunities and supporting process optimization;
- Advising and supporting management and operational teams on quality-related matters.

What do you bring?

- Proven experience in quality management within a logistics or operational environment;
- Knowledge of Quality Management Systems (QMS) and audit methodologies;
- Experience with compliance and continuous improvement;
- Strong analytical and communication skills;
- A proactive, structured and detail-oriented mindset;
- Good command of the English language.
